---
/**
 * The last call to action, and the footer under it.
 *
 * It returns to Day 0 on purpose: the page has just spent Act II arguing about production, and the
 * step it is asking for is still the first command. The same `CtaCommand` the hero uses, so the
 * reader is asked for exactly one thing twice rather than two things once.
 */
import { CtaCommand } from '../../components/CtaCommand';
import { DEMO_URL, SIGN_UP_URL } from './links';
---

<section class="b-close" data-act="none">
  <div class="b-shell">
    <div class="b-close__inner">
      <p class="b-act__kicker">Back to day 0</p>

      <h2 class="b-close__title">Start with the first command.</h2>

      <p class="b-close__lede">
        <code>npx stacktape init</code> reads the repository you already have and writes the config for it. Nothing is
        created on AWS, and nothing is billed, until you say so.
      </p>

      <div class="b-close__cta">
        <CtaCommand client:visible />

        <div class="b-hero__cta-row">
          <a class="b-btn b-btn--solid" href={SIGN_UP_URL}>Sign up</a>
          <a class="b-link-arrow" href={DEMO_URL}>Book a demo<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="b-close__note">
        The CLI and the framework are open source. The Console — the pipelines, the issues, the costs, everything in
        Act II — is the paid product.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
